        }
      ],
      "observation": {
        "results": [
          {
            "source_call_id": "toolu_01Wodh8qEyQe48r9MQX716yq",
            "content": "Web search results for query: \"RAA electric vehicle charging network app Chargefox South Australia\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"EV charging stations\",\"url\":\"https://www.raa.com.au/motor/motoring-services/ev-charging-stations\"},{\"title\":\"Electric vehicles\",\"url\":\"https://www.raa.com.au/motor/ev-hub\"},{\"title\":\"RAA completes South Australia’s first statewide EV charging network - RAA Daily\",\"url\":\"https://daily.raa.com.au/media-resources/raa-completes-south-australias-first-statewide-ev-charging-network/\"},{\"title\":\"First \\\"border-to-border\\\" EV charging network for South Australia launches first 12 sites - The Driven\",\"url\":\"https://thedriven.io/2023/03/02/first-border-to-border-ev-charging-network-for-south-australia-launches-first-12-sites/\"},{\"title\":\"RAA SA Charging Network\",\"url\":\"https://evlog.net.au/raa-sa-charging-network/\"},{\"title\":\"Chargefox builds rapid EV network for South Australians\",\"url\":\"https://www.evcandi.com/news/chargefox-builds-rapid-ev-network-south-australians\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Apps for EVs in Australia\",\"url\":\"https://myevjourney.com/2026/10/27/best-ev-charging-apps-for-evs-in-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"techAU interviews RAA: new South Australia EV charger network feat Kempower, Chargefox, JET Charge\",\"url\":\"https://techau.com.au/techau-interviews-raa-new-south-australia-electric-car-charger-network-feat-kempower-chargefox-jet-charge/\"},{\"title\":\"RAA Charge\",\"url\":\"https://daily.raa.com.au/media-resources/raa-charge-12-electric-vehicle-charging-locations-switched-on-today-as-part-of-network-launch/\"},{\"title\":\"RAA expands EV charging network at four city UPark locations - RAA Daily\",\"url\":\"https://daily.raa.com.au/media-resources/raa-expands-ev-charging-network-at-four-city-upark-locations/\"}]\n\nRAA's charging network in South Australia is called RAA Charge. It runs entirely on the Chargefox app, which you use to find a charger, start it and pay.\n\n**How the app fits in**\n- You find a site, charge and pay in the Chargefox app, or with an RFID card. Step 1: download Chargefox for iOS or Android. Step 2: find your nearest RAA Charge site in the app or on RAA's interactive map. Step 3: charge your EV and pay through the app or with your RFID card.\n- RAA's own member app shows charger locations, details and prices on a map, but you can't use it to start a charge. Any RFID card added to your Chargefox app will work.\n- Chargefox belongs to Australian Motoring Services (AMS) and provides the software, driver support and management services for the network.\n\n**Network size and history**\n- The first 12 sites opened in early 2023, built by Chargefox in partnership with the South Australian Government.\n- RAA says it has completed the network: more than 550 plugs at 144 charging sites, from Yalata to Mount Gambier. The State Government gave RAA a $12.35 million grant to build and run it.\n- RAA calls it SA's largest electric vehicle charging network. A third-party site counted 59 DC charging locations and 142 sites with AC charging (from RAA's charger locator, 1-8-2026).\n\n**Pricing and fees**\n- RAA members get 10% off, but only if a valid membership number is added to their Chargefox profile before the charging session starts.\n- Member prices are Metro AC 40c/kWh at peak (5pm–10pm) and 33c/kWh off-peak; Metro DC 75c/66c; Country AC 42c/35c; Country DC 76c/68c.\n- Idle fees apply at all DC rapid sites in SA. After a 10-minute grace period once charging finishes, it's $1 per minute if you stay plugged in.\n\n**Hardware**\n- AC sites (7kW–22kW) have Type 2 sockets, so you need your own cable. DC sites (60–200kW) have cables attached.\n- Rapid and ultra-rapid chargers use CCS 2 plugs, and some sites also have CHAdeMO.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.",
            "extra": {
              "line": 130,
              "unified_event": {
                "type": "tool.execution_complete",
                "timestamp": "2026-11-19T11:45:10.245Z",
                "data": {
                  "toolCallId": "toolu_01Wodh8qEyQe48r9MQX716yq",
                  "toolName": "WebSearch",
                  "output": "Web search results for query: \"RAA electric vehicle charging network app Chargefox South Australia\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"EV charging stations\",\"url\":\"https://www.raa.com.au/motor/motoring-services/ev-charging-stations\"},{\"title\":\"Electric vehicles\",\"url\":\"https://www.raa.com.au/motor/ev-hub\"},{\"title\":\"RAA completes South Australia’s first statewide EV charging network - RAA Daily\",\"url\":\"https://daily.raa.com.au/media-resources/raa-completes-south-australias-first-statewide-ev-charging-network/\"},{\"title\":\"First \\\"border-to-border\\\" EV charging network for South Australia launches first 12 sites - The Driven\",\"url\":\"https://thedriven.io/2023/03/02/first-border-to-border-ev-charging-network-for-south-australia-launches-first-12-sites/\"},{\"title\":\"RAA SA Charging Network\",\"url\":\"https://evlog.net.au/raa-sa-charging-network/\"},{\"title\":\"Chargefox builds rapid EV network for South Australians\",\"url\":\"https://www.evcandi.com/news/chargefox-builds-rapid-ev-network-south-australians\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Apps for EVs in Australia\",\"url\":\"https://myevjourney.com/2026/10/27/best-ev-charging-apps-for-evs-in-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"techAU interviews RAA: new South Australia EV charger network feat Kempower, Chargefox, JET Charge\",\"url\":\"https://techau.com.au/techau-interviews-raa-new-south-australia-electric-car-charger-network-feat-kempower-chargefox-jet-charge/\"},{\"title\":\"RAA Charge\",\"url\":\"https://daily.raa.com.au/media-resources/raa-charge-12-electric-vehicle-charging-locations-switched-on-today-as-part-of-network-launch/\"},{\"title\":\"RAA expands EV charging network at four city UPark locations - RAA Daily\",\"url\":\"https://daily.raa.com.au/media-resources/raa-expands-ev-charging-network-at-four-city-upark-locations/\"}]\n\nRAA's charging network in South Australia is called RAA Charge. It runs entirely on the Chargefox app, which you use to find a charger, start it and pay.\n\n**How the app fits in**\n- You find a site, charge and pay in the Chargefox app, or with an RFID card. Step 1: download Chargefox for iOS or Android. Step 2: find your nearest RAA Charge site in the app or on RAA's interactive map. Step 3: charge your EV and pay through the app or with your RFID card.\n- RAA's own member app shows charger locations, details and prices on a map, but you can't use it to start a charge. Any RFID card added to your Chargefox app will work.\n- Chargefox belongs to Australian Motoring Services (AMS) and provides the software, driver support and management services for the network.\n\n**Network size and history**\n- The first 12 sites opened in early 2023, built by Chargefox in partnership with the South Australian Government.\n- RAA says it has completed the network: more than 550 plugs at 144 charging sites, from Yalata to Mount Gambier. The State Government gave RAA a $12.35 million grant to build and run it.\n- RAA calls it SA's largest electric vehicle charging network. A third-party site counted 59 DC charging locations and 142 sites with AC charging (from RAA's charger locator, 1-8-2026).\n\n**Pricing and fees**\n- RAA members get 10% off, but only if a valid membership number is added to their Chargefox profile before the charging session starts.\n- Member prices are Metro AC 40c/kWh at peak (5pm–10pm) and 33c/kWh off-peak; Metro DC 75c/66c; Country AC 42c/35c; Country DC 76c/68c.\n- Idle fees apply at all DC rapid sites in SA. After a 10-minute grace period once charging finishes, it's $1 per minute if you stay plugged in.\n\n**Hardware**\n- AC sites (7kW–22kW) have Type 2 sockets, so you need your own cable. DC sites (60–200kW) have cables attached.\n- Rapid and ultra-rapid chargers use CCS 2 plugs, and some sites also have CHAdeMO.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.",
