    {
      "step_id": 205,
      "timestamp": "2026-11-19T11:45:43.929Z",
      "source": "agent",
      "message": "",
      "tool_calls": [
        {
          "tool_call_id": "toolu_01RX4fQYSt7i1yxBRz7qdSom",
          "function_name": "WebFetch",
          "arguments": {
            "prompt": "What prices per kWh does this page give for Exploren DC fast chargers, with dates and how the data was gathered? Quote exact figures, any typical/median figure.",
            "url": "https://costtocharge.com.au/public-charging-prices/exploren/"
          }
        }
      ],
      "observation": {
        "results": [
          {
            "source_call_id": "toolu_01RX4fQYSt7i1yxBRz7qdSom",
            "content": "**Exploren prices on this page**\n\nThe page doesn't split prices into DC fast and AC charging. Only one site is clearly labelled as DC:\n\n- **UTAS Shed Building - Public DC (Launceston, TAS):** \"70c/kWh base\". The idle fee is 100c/min after a 10-minute grace period, and the connection fee is $0.00.\n\nThe other three named sites aren't identified by charger type:\n\n- Toronto Commercial Centre Carpark, NSW: 35c/kWh, plus a $0.30 connection fee\n- Kingston Village Square, VIC: 55c/kWh\n- Cairns Night Markets, QLD: 60c/kWh\n\nAcross all four sites, the page says energy costs \"$0.35 to $0.70 per kWh\". It gives **no typical or median figure**, only this range. For a 40 kWh stop, that works out to $14.00–$28.00 before fees.\n\n**Dates**\n\nEvery site row was checked on 24 October 2026. One vehicle capacity source oddly shows a check date of 2026-11-13, which is later than the page's stated check date.\n\n**How the data was gathered**\n\nThe prices come from Exploren's public charger-finder listings, with each row linked to its source. The page says it captures \"published source information rather than an account-specific app quote or a visit to the charger.\" None of the sources stated time bands or member pricing, and parking charges weren't verified.",
            "extra": {
              "line": 234,
              "unified_event": {
                "type": "tool.execution_complete",
                "timestamp": "2026-11-19T11:45:51.217Z",
                "data": {
                  "toolCallId": "toolu_01RX4fQYSt7i1yxBRz7qdSom",
                  "toolName": "WebFetch",
                  "output": "**Exploren prices on this page**\n\nThe page doesn't split prices into DC fast and AC charging. Only one site is clearly labelled as DC:\n\n- **UTAS Shed Building - Public DC (Launceston, TAS):** \"70c/kWh base\". The idle fee is 100c/min after a 10-minute grace period, and the connection fee is $0.00.\n\nThe other three named sites aren't identified by charger type:\n\n- Toronto Commercial Centre Carpark, NSW: 35c/kWh, plus a $0.30 connection fee\n- Kingston Village Square, VIC: 55c/kWh\n- Cairns Night Markets, QLD: 60c/kWh\n\nAcross all four sites, the page says energy costs \"$0.35 to $0.70 per kWh\". It gives **no typical or median figure**, only this range. For a 40 kWh stop, that works out to $14.00–$28.00 before fees.\n\n**Dates**\n\nEvery site row was checked on 24 October 2026. One vehicle capacity source oddly shows a check date of 2026-11-13, which is later than the page's stated check date.\n\n**How the data was gathered**\n\nThe prices come from Exploren's public charger-finder listings, with each row linked to its source. The page says it captures \"published source information rather than an account-specific app quote or a visit to the charger.\" None of the sources stated time bands or member pricing, and parking charges weren't verified.",
