            "content": "Web search results for query: \"WeVolt EV charging Western Australia app price per kWh\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Transperth Electric Vehicle Charger Trial\",\"url\":\"https://www.mysaytransport.wa.gov.au/pta-ev-chargers\"},{\"title\":\"Charging Fees, the Service Fee and the Platform Fee (for Operators) — Wevolt Support\",\"url\":\"https://wevolt.com.au/support/kb/charging-fees-and-the-service-fee-for-operators\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Costs in Australia\",\"url\":\"https://myevjourney.com/2026/01/01/ev-charging-costs-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"Is a Home EV Charger Worth It in WA? (Cost & ROI Guide) - Electric Vehicle Charging Installations\",\"url\":\"https://evci.com.au/is-a-home-ev-charger-worth-it-in-wa/\"},{\"title\":\"For drivers — how charging works\",\"url\":\"https://wevolt.com.au/drivers\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Costs in Australia\",\"url\":\"https://myevjourney.com/2025/09/20/ev-charging-costs-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Costs in Australia\",\"url\":\"https://myevjourney.com/2025/12/23/ev-charging-costs-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"How Much Does It Cost to Charge an EV in Australia? (2026)\",\"url\":\"https://evcharginglocations.com.au/blog/ev-charging-cost-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"Wevolt - App Store - Apple\",\"url\":\"https://apps.apple.com/au/app/wevolt/id6446931550\"},{\"title\":\"Market-leading software for EV charging\",\"url\":\"https://www.wevolt.com.au/home-1\"}]\n\nWevolt doesn't have one network-wide price per kWh. Each charger's owner sets its own price, so cost varies by site. The one specific WA figure I found is 43c/kWh at the Transperth chargers.\n\n- **How pricing works:** Wevolt runs the app, network and payments. The chargers themselves belong to independent operators — businesses, councils, property owners and workplaces — who list them in the app and set their own prices. Operators can charge per kWh, per minute, as a flat fee, or with a free period, plus any idle fee. On top of that, Wevolt adds its own Service Fee, which drivers pay. The help article doesn't say how much it is.\n- **New platform fee:** For sessions that start from 00:00 AWST on 13 October 2026, Wevolt keeps a Platform Fee of 4% of the charging cost. It's taken out of the operator's payout, not added to what drivers pay.\n- **Transperth trial (WA example):** Wevolt runs the Public Transport Authority's chargers, which charge at up to 7kW, taking approximately eight hours to charge a typical EV. The charging fee is a usage charge of $0.43 per kWh. That page is about 9 months old.\n- **Price ranges from MyEVJourney (Australia-wide, not just WA):** A table from January 2026 lists Wevolt DC at 35 to 73 c/kWh. A December 2025 version listed 45 to 75. A September 2025 version listed Wevolt overall at 0 to 65 c/kWh, with some free chargers.\n- **WA context:** A 2026 WA guide puts public AC chargers at roughly 10–40 cents per kWh and DC fast chargers at roughly 40–70 cents.\n- **Paying in the app:** A pre-authorisation hold is placed on your card, then you're billed for the energy used. The app shows live availability and pricing for each charger, so the app is the only place to see the current price at a specific site.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.",
            "extra": {
              "line": 273,
              "unified_event": {
                "type": "tool.execution_complete",
                "timestamp": "2026-11-19T11:46:14.730Z",
                "data": {
                  "toolCallId": "toolu_01JLu1gmv7qBeyAeoJnMj2KX",
                  "toolName": "WebSearch",
                  "output": "Web search results for query: \"WeVolt EV charging Western Australia app price per kWh\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Transperth Electric Vehicle Charger Trial\",\"url\":\"https://www.mysaytransport.wa.gov.au/pta-ev-chargers\"},{\"title\":\"Charging Fees, the Service Fee and the Platform Fee (for Operators) — Wevolt Support\",\"url\":\"https://wevolt.com.au/support/kb/charging-fees-and-the-service-fee-for-operators\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Costs in Australia\",\"url\":\"https://myevjourney.com/2026/01/01/ev-charging-costs-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"Is a Home EV Charger Worth It in WA? (Cost & ROI Guide) - Electric Vehicle Charging Installations\",\"url\":\"https://evci.com.au/is-a-home-ev-charger-worth-it-in-wa/\"},{\"title\":\"For drivers — how charging works\",\"url\":\"https://wevolt.com.au/drivers\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Costs in Australia\",\"url\":\"https://myevjourney.com/2025/09/20/ev-charging-costs-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Costs in Australia\",\"url\":\"https://myevjourney.com/2025/12/23/ev-charging-costs-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"How Much Does It Cost to Charge an EV in Australia? (2026)\",\"url\":\"https://evcharginglocations.com.au/blog/ev-charging-cost-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"Wevolt - App Store - Apple\",\"url\":\"https://apps.apple.com/au/app/wevolt/id6446931550\"},{\"title\":\"Market-leading software for EV charging\",\"url\":\"https://www.wevolt.com.au/home-1\"}]\n\nWevolt doesn't have one network-wide price per kWh. Each charger's owner sets its own price, so cost varies by site. The one specific WA figure I found is 43c/kWh at the Transperth chargers.\n\n- **How pricing works:** Wevolt runs the app, network and payments. The chargers themselves belong to independent operators — businesses, councils, property owners and workplaces — who list them in the app and set their own prices. Operators can charge per kWh, per minute, as a flat fee, or with a free period, plus any idle fee. On top of that, Wevolt adds its own Service Fee, which drivers pay. The help article doesn't say how much it is.\n- **New platform fee:** For sessions that start from 00:00 AWST on 13 October 2026, Wevolt keeps a Platform Fee of 4% of the charging cost. It's taken out of the operator's payout, not added to what drivers pay.\n- **Transperth trial (WA example):** Wevolt runs the Public Transport Authority's chargers, which charge at up to 7kW, taking approximately eight hours to charge a typical EV. The charging fee is a usage charge of $0.43 per kWh. That page is about 9 months old.\n- **Price ranges from MyEVJourney (Australia-wide, not just WA):** A table from January 2026 lists Wevolt DC at 35 to 73 c/kWh. A December 2025 version listed 45 to 75. A September 2025 version listed Wevolt overall at 0 to 65 c/kWh, with some free chargers.\n- **WA context:** A 2026 WA guide puts public AC chargers at roughly 10–40 cents per kWh and DC fast chargers at roughly 40–70 cents.\n- **Paying in the app:** A pre-authorisation hold is placed on your card, then you're billed for the energy used. The app shows live availability and pricing for each charger, so the app is the only place to see the current price at a specific site.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.",
