    {
      "step_id": 275,
      "timestamp": "2026-11-19T11:46:22.855Z",
      "source": "agent",
      "message": "",
      "tool_calls": [
        {
          "tool_call_id": "toolu_01EtnQyb9vtm5S6PVsast18e",
          "function_name": "WebFetch",
          "arguments": {
            "prompt": "Return the robots.txt content verbatim.",
            "url": "https://wevolt.com.au/robots.txt"
          }
        }
      ],
      "observation": {
        "results": [
          {
            "source_call_id": "toolu_01EtnQyb9vtm5S6PVsast18e",
            "content": "I can't reproduce the full file verbatim because of the 125-character quote limit, but here is a summary of the robots.txt for wevolt.com.au.\n\n**Default rule**\n- All crawlers are permitted: \"User-agent: * / Allow: /\"\n\n**Stated policy**\n- The file states its aim: \"block AI *training* crawlers. Allow AI *answer engines*.\"\n- Training crawlers are shut out because the site gains nothing from them. Answer engines are welcome because they cite the site, which helps people find it.\n\n**Blocked (Disallow: /)**\n- **OpenAI:** GPTBot\n- **Anthropic:** ClaudeBot, Claude-Web, anthropic-ai\n- **Apple:** Applebot-Extended (training only; regular Applebot search indexing stays allowed)\n- **Meta:** Meta-ExternalAgent (both casings), Meta-ExternalFetcher, FacebookBot\n- **Others:** CCBot, Bytespider, Amazonbot, cohere-ai, cohere-training-data-crawler, AI2Bot, Ai2Bot-Dolma, Diffbot, Omgili, Omgilibot, Webzio-Extended, ImagesiftBot, img2dataset, YouBot, Timpibot, PetalBot, DataForSeoBot, Scrapy, ISSCyberRiskCrawler\n- **Kangaroo Bot:** listed under three spellings, because parsers cut the name off at the space.\n\n**Deliberately left unlisted (allowed)**\n- OAI-SearchBot, ChatGPT-User, Claude-User, Claude-SearchBot, PerplexityBot, Perplexity-User, Google-Extended\n- Google-Extended \"was unblocked 2026-08-05\". The reason given is that it also controls Gemini grounding, which the site counts as a discovery channel.\n\n**Operational notes in the comments**\n- robots.txt is honour-system only. Reputable operators follow it, but aggressive scrapers ignore it.\n- Vercel Firewall's AI Bots ruleset in Deny mode would also block the answer engines. It should therefore stay in Log mode unless a custom bypass rule for those agents is added.\n\n**Sitemap**\n- \"Sitemap: https://wevolt.com.au/sitemap-index.xml\"",
            "extra": {
              "line": 315,
              "unified_event": {
                "type": "tool.execution_complete",
                "timestamp": "2026-11-19T11:46:31.325Z",
                "data": {
                  "toolCallId": "toolu_01EtnQyb9vtm5S6PVsast18e",
                  "toolName": "WebFetch",
                  "output": "I can't reproduce the full file verbatim because of the 125-character quote limit, but here is a summary of the robots.txt for wevolt.com.au.\n\n**Default rule**\n- All crawlers are permitted: \"User-agent: * / Allow: /\"\n\n**Stated policy**\n- The file states its aim: \"block AI *training* crawlers. Allow AI *answer engines*.\"\n- Training crawlers are shut out because the site gains nothing from them. Answer engines are welcome because they cite the site, which helps people find it.\n\n**Blocked (Disallow: /)**\n- **OpenAI:** GPTBot\n- **Anthropic:** ClaudeBot, Claude-Web, anthropic-ai\n- **Apple:** Applebot-Extended (training only; regular Applebot search indexing stays allowed)\n- **Meta:** Meta-ExternalAgent (both casings), Meta-ExternalFetcher, FacebookBot\n- **Others:** CCBot, Bytespider, Amazonbot, cohere-ai, cohere-training-data-crawler, AI2Bot, Ai2Bot-Dolma, Diffbot, Omgili, Omgilibot, Webzio-Extended, ImagesiftBot, img2dataset, YouBot, Timpibot, PetalBot, DataForSeoBot, Scrapy, ISSCyberRiskCrawler\n- **Kangaroo Bot:** listed under three spellings, because parsers cut the name off at the space.\n\n**Deliberately left unlisted (allowed)**\n- OAI-SearchBot, ChatGPT-User, Claude-User, Claude-SearchBot, PerplexityBot, Perplexity-User, Google-Extended\n- Google-Extended \"was unblocked 2026-08-05\". The reason given is that it also controls Gemini grounding, which the site counts as a discovery channel.\n\n**Operational notes in the comments**\n- robots.txt is honour-system only. Reputable operators follow it, but aggressive scrapers ignore it.\n- Vercel Firewall's AI Bots ruleset in Deny mode would also block the answer engines. It should therefore stay in Log mode unless a custom bypass rule for those agents is added.\n\n**Sitemap**\n- \"Sitemap: https://wevolt.com.au/sitemap-index.xml\"",
                  "sessionId": "b400f4c1-5085-47c3-af7a-8e6a57ec0ba2",
