    {
      "step_id": 448,
      "timestamp": "2026-11-19T11:47:54.004Z",
      "source": "agent",
      "message": "I've opened a pull request for `networks.json` that adds two networks and connects every one of the 12 unmatched operators to a network. No typical prices changed. Both `format.mjs` and `validate.mjs` pass.\n\n**New networks** (both have no typical price yet, because no source I'm allowed to read gives one):\n- **Exploren** also covers **Engie**: Exploren's parent company bought Engie's Australian chargers in 2025 and moved them into the Exploren app. Its site is set to `forbidden`, since we may not read Exploren's own website.\n- **Wevolt** also covers **Electrona**, whose Tasmanian chargers take a card or the Wevolt app. Its site is set to `unchecked`: Wevolt's robots.txt blocks AI training crawlers, and I didn't read its terms.\n\n**Added to existing networks:**\n- **Chargefox:** Yurika and the Queensland Electric Super Highway (49 and 6 sites), RAA, Electric Highway Tasmania, the WA EV Network and Horizon Power's EV Highway, and Woolworths. Each is paid through Chargefox's app.\n- **Evie:** Charging the Regions, whose chargers Evie runs.\n\n**Prices:**\n- I found nothing I'm allowed to use that shows a new typical price. The Evie FAQ gives only cost per full charge, and the NRMA and Horizon Power pages refused to load.\n- Every `checked` date is 2026-10-27, under six months old, so I opened no issue asking you to check prices in the apps.\n\n**Things to check before merging:**\n- **`raa` is a short match.** Any site name containing \"raa\" would get Chargefox's price. I couldn't search the charger file to rule that out.\n- **`woolworths`** could catch another network's charger in a Woolworths car park, for example an Evie site named after the store.\n- **Charging the Regions:** a few of Wellington Shire's sites use Chargefox rather than Evie, so they'd get Evie's price.\n- **WA EV Network price:** its fees ($0.60/kWh at fast chargers, the same as Chargefox's typical price) came from a search result, not the Horizon Power page itself.\n\nMy notes on all 12 operators are saved in memory (`operators.json`) for the next run.",
      "model_name": "claude-opus-5-5",
      "extra": {
        "line": 486,
        "unified_event": {
          "type": "assistant.message",
          "timestamp": "2026-11-19T11:47:54.004Z",
          "data": {
            "sourceEngine": "claude",
            "content": "I've opened a pull request for `networks.json` that adds two networks and connects every one of the 12 unmatched operators to a network. No typical prices changed. Both `format.mjs` and `validate.mjs` pass.\n\n**New networks** (both have no typical price yet, because no source I'm allowed to read gives one):\n- **Exploren** also covers **Engie**: Exploren's parent company bought Engie's Australian chargers in 2025 and moved them into the Exploren app. Its site is set to `forbidden`, since we may not read Exploren's own website.\n- **Wevolt** also covers **Electrona**, whose Tasmanian chargers take a card or the Wevolt app. Its site is set to `unchecked`: Wevolt's robots.txt blocks AI training crawlers, and I didn't read its terms.\n\n**Added to existing networks:**\n- **Chargefox:** Yurika and the Queensland Electric Super Highway (49 and 6 sites), RAA, Electric Highway Tasmania, the WA EV Network and Horizon Power's EV Highway, and Woolworths. Each is paid through Chargefox's app.\n- **Evie:** Charging the Regions, whose chargers Evie runs.\n\n**Prices:**\n- I found nothing I'm allowed to use that shows a new typical price. The Evie FAQ gives only cost per full charge, and the NRMA and Horizon Power pages refused to load.\n- Every `checked` date is 2026-10-27, under six months old, so I opened no issue asking you to check prices in the apps.\n\n**Things to check before merging:**\n- **`raa` is a short match.** Any site name containing \"raa\" would get Chargefox's price. I couldn't search the charger file to rule that out.\n- **`woolworths`** could catch another network's charger in a Woolworths car park, for example an Evie site named after the store.\n- **Charging the Regions:** a few of Wellington Shire's sites use Chargefox rather than Evie, so they'd get Evie's price.\n- **WA EV Network price:** its fees ($0.60/kWh at fast chargers, the same as Chargefox's typical price) came from a search result, not the Horizon Power page itself.\n\nMy notes on all 12 operators are saved in memory (`operators.json`) for the next run.",
            "messageId": "msg_011ChCEVQifa9mYMeFk9Dhmz",
            "contentIndex": 0,
            "sessionId": "b400f4c1-5085-47c3-af7a-8e6a57ec0ba2",
            "parentToolUseId": null,
            "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
          },
